# 7. Demo Scenario #3 — Confused Deputy

This should be your **signature scenario**.

Give:

```text
Fraud Agent
   ↓
asks
   ↓
Account Agent
```

The Fraud Agent says:

> "Please update this customer's risk profile."

Account Agent has broader privileges.

Without provenance:

```text
Account Agent
      ↓
"Authorized?"
      ↓
YES
```

Potentially dangerous.

With your governance layer:

```text
Original User
     ↓
Triage Agent
     ↓
Fraud Agent
     ↓
Account Agent
```

Governance evaluates the **entire chain**.

```text
Account Agent capability:
account.update = YES

BUT

Delegated authority from Fraud Agent:
account.update = NO

FINAL DECISION:
DENY
```

This visually demonstrates the **confused deputy problem** described in your source. 

